※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4574

※ The compiler holds the number each system call has on each architecture,
※ because the compiler is what knows which architecture it is building for.
※ What is in that table is what the runtime and the standard library ask for,
※ each number checked against the kernel's own; a call nothing has asked for yet
※ is not there, and adding one is a line per architecture rather than anything a
※ program can do.
※
※ A call some architecture has and this one does not reads differently (4575), so
※ a mistyped name and a name that is simply not there are told apart.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let answer: i64 = ⎕syscall(⎕sc@wirte, 1i64)
    if answer < 0i64: 0u6 else: 1u6
